    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have a similar issue so I thought I&#39;d throw in a histogram of p-values for an example.  I have ~112k loci/rows and majority of the loci have a q-value of ~0.38.  I have other pairwise comparisons that I&#39;ve done with different samples where all the q-values are 0.005 even though the p-values cover the range of 0-1 ~~ I can post that example later if necessary   </div><div><br></div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%5BDocument1%5D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132416.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%255BDocument1%255D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132416.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564882000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OLF1DPDKnTidvpk0XmEpp\">pvalue screenshot: </a><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%5BDocument1%5D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132834.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%255BDocument1%255D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132834.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564882000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ptef_3aiZG76zEUZd9bOe\">qvalue screenshot</a> (notice here the log scale of y axis): </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Microsoft_Excel-20140411-133348.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Microsoft_Excel-20140411-133348.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564882000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08HYSsnTqT6s8XGWFlL5Dg\">scatter plot of q-values v p-values</a></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Mac</div></div>"
