    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Wednesday, April 9, 2014 6:50:32 AM UTC-7, Alexis wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Hi, </div><div><br></div><div>Command:<br></div><div><br></div><div>myMethylDiff &lt;- calculateDiffMeth(myMethylBase, num.cores=3)</div></div><div><div>write.table(myMethylDiff, file=file.path(outputDirectory,  &quot;methylation_differences_slim.tsv&quot;), quote=FALSE, row.names=FALSE, sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>Output:</div><div><br></div><div>Note the repeating q-values. They are always 0.15... or 0.13… throughout the entire file, despite the p-values and the methylation differences values being different.</div><div>What does that mean.</div><div><br></div><div>chr<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>start<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>end<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>strand<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>pvalue<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>qvalue<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>meth.diff</div><div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3053153<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3053153<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0.68610731364818<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0.159516627181397<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>-1.28998968008256</div><div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3053199<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3053199<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0.338761893722175<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0.136993870339041<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0.680272108843537</div><div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3053211<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3053211<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>0.705519721525744<span style=\"whit