  {
   "id": "poFJbwQtDQgJ",
   "from": "Altuna Akalin",
   "author": "ab8277113f65c05e",
   "date": "2014-04-15T08:13:00Z",
   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] Re: Repeating q-values when calculating methylation differences",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">please refer to the SLIM paper, we are using the same source code with no adjustments on default parameters or the code, you will see examples of distributions where simulation and tests were based on. Since it doesn&#39;t always work without adjusting the parameters in the extreme cases we put an alternative, slim=FALSE (maybe it should even be the default).  I think in your case it could be a problem of non-uniform coverage over p-values, i.e. gaps in the histogram. Just use slim=FALSE when in doubt. <div>\r\n<br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Altuna</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Apr 14, 2014 at 9:17 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">macg...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for your reply. I wanted to give this more extreme example too.  Here, there are ~22k loci and although the pvalues cover the range of 0 -1, the q-values are all 0.0054 (see screenshots below).  This doesn&#39;t make sense to me how a qvalue would be &lt;0.01 with a p value of 1.  Here, if slim=FALSE all of the q values = 1.  You mentioned the method expects a certain distribution of p values - what type of distribution is it? A normal distribution or something else? --Thanks for your help.</div>\r\n<div><br></div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%5BDocument1%5D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140414-121159.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%255BDocument1%255D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140414-121159.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ClSs2tjOTwn1B2253IeN7\">p value screenshot</a><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%5BDocument1%5D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140414-121257.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%255BDocument1%255D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140414-121257.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2rF4RnfNFzoRZn_O0SAReB\">q value screenshoot</a> (the screenshot is rather silly since all 22k=0.0054)<div>\r\n<br><br>On Friday, April 11, 2014 4:03:26 PM UTC-7, Altuna Akalin wrote:</div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, this could be the same issue. How does it look when slim=FALSE (it is more robust), as I said the method expects a certain distribution, and you have very few or no significant P-values.<div>\r\n<br></div><div>\r\nBest,</div><div>Altuna</div></div></div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div><div>On Fri, Apr 11, 2014 at 10:37 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">macg...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have a similar issue so I thought I&#39;d throw in a histogram of p-values for an example.  I have ~112k loci/rows and majority of the loci have a q-value of ~0.38.  I have other pairwise comparisons that I&#39;ve done with different samples where all the q-values are 0.005 even though the p-values cover the range of 0-1 ~~ I can post that example later if necessary   </div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%5BDocument1%5D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132416.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%255BDocument1%255D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132416.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rMpgeIFKwVo-2sZjqVIeA\">pvalue screenshot: </a><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%5BDocument1%5D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132834.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Output1_%255BDocument1%255D_-_IBM_SPSS_Statistics_Viewer-20140411-132834.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0uCmJpm4F6IUiWFmX5lK5q\">qvalue screenshot</a> (notice here the log scale of y axis): </div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Microsoft_Excel-20140411-133348.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eagle.fish.washington.edu/bivalvia/skitch/Microsoft_Excel-20140411-133348.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EtMYxOEzCPrU1eaagIIQ2\">scatter plot of q-values v p-values</a></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<div>Mac<div><div><br><br>On Wednesday, April 9, 2014 6:50:32 AM UTC-7, Alexis wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div><div>Hi, </div><div><br></div><div>Command:<br></div><div><br></div><div>myMethylDiff &lt;- calculateDiffMeth(<u></u>myMethylBase<u></u>, num.cores=3)</div></div><div><div>write.table(myMethylDiff, file=file.path(<u></u>outputDirectory<u></u>,  &quot;methylation_differences_<u></u>slim<u></u>.tsv&quot;), quote=FALSE, row.names=FALSE, sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)</div>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>Output:</div><div><br></div><div>Note the repeating q-values. They are always 0.15... or 0.13… throughout the entire file, despite the p-values and the methylation differences values being different.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>What does that mean.</div><div><br></div><div>chr<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>start<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>end<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>strand<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>pvalue<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>qvalue<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>meth.diff</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053153<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053153<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.68610731364818<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.159516627181397<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-1.28998968008256</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053199<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053199<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.338761893722175<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.136993870339041<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.680272108843537</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053211<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053211<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.705519721525744<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.159516627181397<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-0.465700768775872</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053217<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053217<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.0557017740355649<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.136993870339041<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>4.6031746031746</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053226<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053226<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.151669708480166<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.136993870339041<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-2.43055555555556</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053256<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053256<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.734443355978505<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.159516627181397<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-0.488400488400489</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053289<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053289<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.159516627181397<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053294<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>3053294<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.625545693510334<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.159516627181397<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>-1.09805924412666</div>\r\n\r\n<div>….</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you for your help, </div><div><br></div><div>Alexis</div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div><div><div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;methylkit_discussion&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_discussion+<u></u>unsub...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></div></div>\r\n\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">methylkit_...@<u></u>googlegroups.com</a>.<div><br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/methylkit_discussion&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bw8qIUlxzNfDo8RxiMUL6\">http://groups.google.com/<u></u>group/methylkit_discussion</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234564907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DpetqJfMzSSFIYD3u_T8C\">https://groups.google.com/d/<u></u>optout</a>.<br>\r\n</div></div></div></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
